            "title": "Flight cuts, consumer sentiment, Miran speech: What to Watch",
            "description": "<p>Market Domination Overtime host <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/josh-lipton/\">Josh Lipton</a> takes a look at the top stories for investors to watch on Friday, Nov. 7.</p>\n<p>The Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) announced a 10% decrease in air traffic, going into effect on Friday at 40 major airports.</p>\n<p>More commentary is coming from several Federal Reserve officials, including New York Fed President John Williams and Fed Governor Stephen Miran.</p>\n<p>Constellation Energy (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/CEG\">CEG</a>), Enbridge (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/ENB\">ENB</a>), and Duke Energy (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/DUK\">DUK</a>) will report quarterly results in the morning.</p>\n<p>The University of Michigan's preliminary November consumer sentiment reading will be posted in the morning.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more <a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-domination-overtime/\">Market Domination Overtime</a>.</p>",
